  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Addition of alc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KOH</mi></math> to haloalkanes follows the Saytzeff rule which points towards greater stability. Saytzeff&#39;s rule implies that elimination reactions favour formation of alkene with greater number of substituents.<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0186_9f9756c42cc2.png\" style=\"width: 185px; height: 75px;\" /><br /><br />Not only that, but it also gives the molecule an extended conjugate system which further enhances its stability.</p>"
